---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Colophon — Jonathan Tollefson"
  description="How this portfolio site is built. Astro, Notion, Vercel, and a resume versioning system that ships new variants without code changes."
>
  <main class="cl">
    <header class="cl-header">
      <div class="inner">
        <a class="back" href="/">← Index</a>
        <p class="num">Colophon</p>
        <h1 class="title">A site built to demonstrate the system that built it.</h1>
      </div>
    </header>

    <article class="cl-body">
      <div class="inner prose">
        <h2>Stack</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Astro</strong> for static site generation, TypeScript strict throughout.</li>
          <li><strong>Notion</strong> as the content layer. Two databases: Case Studies, Resumes.</li>
          <li><strong>Vercel</strong> for deployment and SSL.</li>
          <li><strong>Geist Variable</strong>, self-hosted via Fontsource.</li>
          <li><strong>CSS custom properties</strong> for the four chromatic themes.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Content</h2>
        <p>
          Case studies and resumes both live as rows in Notion databases. The
          build queries Notion at compile time, normalizes each row into typed
          objects, and renders Notion's block tree as editorial prose. Image
          galleries auto-pull from <code>/public/case-studies/[slug]/</code>.
          Drop in a file, it appears.
        </p>

        <h2>Resume system</h2>
        <p>
          A Master row plus per-role variants. Each row carries <code>Slug</code>,
          <code>Status</code>, <code>Tailored For</code>, and an <code>Is Default</code>
          flag, plus full Notion content. The Master renders at <code>/resume</code>.
          Variants render at <code>/resume/[slug]</code> for direct sharing
          with recruiters.
        </p>
        <p>
          Adding a new tailored resume for a new role is one new database row,
          edited and saved in Notion. The site picks up the new variant on the
          next deploy. No code change. No file edit. The route auto-generates
          from <code>getStaticPaths()</code>.
        </p>

        <h2>Themes</h2>
        <p>
          Four palettes (Carbon, Powder, Field, Honey) scoped to a
          <code>[data-theme]</code> attribute on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>. The
          theme selector mutates the attribute; the entire site reflows in one
          repaint via CSS custom property cascade. Press <kbd>T</kbd> from
          anywhere to cycle.
        </p>
        <p>
          The speckled cardstock background, the cursor accent, the
          tagline rule, and every typographic surface inherit from the same
          token set. No theme hardcodes a color.
        </p>

        <h2>Print stylesheet</h2>
        <p>
          The resume route has a print stylesheet that forces white background,
          black text, letter size, and one-page typography. <kbd>Cmd+P</kbd> on
          <code>/resume/delta-srux</code> produces a clean PDF ready to send.
        </p>

        <h2>Source</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="https://github.com/ai-tolo/jt-portfolio" rel="noopener">github.com/ai-tolo/jt-portfolio</a>
          — public. Built May 2026 with Claude Code on an M3 Air, replacing an
          aging Framer portfolio.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <nav class="cl-nav">
      <div class="inner">
        <a class="back" href="/">← Back to index</a>
      </div>
    </nav>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .cl {
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  .cl-header {
    padding: var(--space-12) 0 var(--space-12);
  }
  .back {
    font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-eyebrow);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }
  .num {
    font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-eyebrow);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-display);
    line-height: 1.05;
    max-width: 22ch;
  }

  .cl-body {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-16);
  }
  .prose {
    max-width: 64ch;
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-eyebrow);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .prose p {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .prose ul {
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }
  .prose li::marker {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .prose code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--surface-1);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .prose kbd {
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 0.85em;
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    color: var(--text);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--surface-1);
  }
  .prose a {
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .prose a:hover {
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  }

  .cl-nav {
    padding: var(--space-12) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
</style>
